From d1463bff31c93d410387e187771afe45ff409f7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 11:13:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 20/36] ggml: add the missing INDEXER_FILL entry to
 GGML_OP_NAME

GGML_OP_INDEXER_FILL was added to the enum (delivery block 14) but not to the
GGML_OP_NAME table, so every op from INDEXER_FILL onward was shifted by one and
ggml_op_name() returned the wrong name -- e.g. UNARY logged as MAP_CUSTOM1.  This
is a delivery bug (present in the 8a2567e1e base, not introduced by this WIP); it
is cosmetic in the delivery (ggml_op_name is only used for logging) but it
mislabeled the MMB_CVT analysis.  Move it into the delivery when the WIP is
promoted.
---
 ggml/src/ggml.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml.c b/ggml/src/ggml.c
index bd4e2aabb..6956028f4 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml.c
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml.c
@@ -1087,6 +1087,7 @@ static const char * GGML_OP_NAME[GGML_OP_COUNT] = {
     "FLASH_ATTN_QSA",
     "INDEXER_TOPK",
     "INDEXER_SCORE",
+    "INDEXER_FILL",
     "HC_MIX",
     "HC_COMBINE",
 
